    {
      "id": "warehouse_analogy",
      "duration": "43s",
      "layout": {"type": "center", "gap": "large", "align": "center"},
      "auto_visible": false,
      "show_progress_bar": false,
      "narration": "Think of Broker A and Broker B as two different storefronts. The fund can shop at either one. But after it buys something, it wants the accepted purchase sent to one receiving warehouse, where the inventory and the bill can be managed together. That receiving warehouse is the useful mental model for a prime broker. The analogy is not exact. Securities move electronically, not in boxes. But it gives us the central idea. Executing brokers help the fund make trades. A prime broker helps the fund operate and finance the accepted positions that result from those trades.",
      "objects": [
        {
