    {
      "id": "harbor_short_and_borrow",
      "duration": "42s",
      "layout": {"type": "center", "gap": "large", "align": "center"},
      "auto_visible": false,
      "show_progress_bar": false,
      "narration": "Now suppose the fund believes Harbor will fall. It wants to sell 40 Harbor shares now and buy them back later. But the fund does not own those shares, so it cannot simply pretend they exist. It needs to borrow them. Before Broker B executes the short, it must determine that shares can be borrowed for delivery. Then a stock-loan arrangement supports that borrowing while the short stays open, often through the prime broker or its lending partners. That is why the prime account shows two facts together: short 40 Harbor, and borrowed 40 Harbor. The short can remain open only while the borrow is available.",
      "objects": [
        {
          "type": "group",
          "id": "harbor_world",
          "layout": {"type": "stack", "gap": "large", "align": "center"},
          "visible": true,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "group",
              "id": "harbor_actor_row",
              "layout": {"type": "flow", "direction": "horizontal", "gap": "large", "align": "center"},
              "visible": true,
              "children": [
                {"type": "semantic_icon", "id": "fund", "actor_id": "fund", "continuity_mode": "position_only", "icon_name": "fund", "content": "Fund", "style": "focus-coral", "size_variant": "hero", "visible": true},
                {"type": "semantic_icon", "id": "broker_b", "actor_id": "broker_b", "continuity_mode": "position_only", "icon_name": "storefront", "content": "Broker B", "style": "focus-cyan", "size_variant": "hero", "visible": true},
                {"type": "semantic_icon", "id": "prime_broker", "actor_id": "prime_broker", "continuity_mode": "position_only", "icon_name": "warehouse", "content": "Prime broker", "style": "focus-gold", "size_variant": "hero", "visible": true}
              ]
            },
            {"type": "box", "id": "harbor_intent", "content": "Sell 40 Harbor", "style": "focus-coral", "size_variant": "hero", "visible": false},
            {"type": "token", "id": "harbor_buyback", "content": "Buy back later", "style": "focus-coral", "size_variant": "hero", "visible": false},
            {"type": "text", "id": "borrow_question", "content": "40 shares needed", "style": "heading", "visible": false},
            {
              "type": "group",
              "id": "harbor_pair",
              "layout": {"type": "flow", "direction": "horizontal", "gap": "medium", "align": "center"},
              "visible": true,
              "children": [
                {"type": "box", "id": "short_harbor", "actor_id": "short_harbor", "continuity_mode": "position_only", "content": "Short 40 Harbor", "style": "focus-coral", "size_variant": "hero", "visible": false},
                {"type": "text", "id": "paired_with", "content": "paired with", "style": "operator", "visible": false},
                {"type": "semantic_icon", "id": "borrowed_harbor", "actor_id": "borrowed_harbor", "continuity_mode": "position_only", "icon_name": "borrow", "content": "Borrowed 40 Harbor", "style": "focus-gold", "size_variant": "hero", "visible": false}
              ]
            },
            {"type": "connector", "id": "borrow_route", "from": "prime_broker", "to": "borrowed_harbor", "style": "gold", "visible": false}
          ]
        }
      ],
      "animations": [
        {"id": "show_harbor_intent", "action": "fade-in", "target": "harbor_intent", "at": "6s", "cue": "sell 40 Harbor shares now", "duration": "0.9s"},
        {"id": "show_buyback", "action": "fade-in", "target": "harbor_buyback", "at": "11s", "cue": "buy them back later", "duration": "0.7s"},
        {"id": "show_borrow_question", "action": "fade-in", "target": "borrow_question", "at": "14s", "cue": "needs to borrow them", "duration": "0.8s"},
        {"id": "move_short_to_broker", "action": "move-to", "target": "harbor_intent", "to_id": "broker_b", "at": "19s", "cue": "Before Broker B executes the short", "duration": "1s", "translate": {"x": -0.65, "y": 0, "basis": "target"}},
        {"id": "draw_borrow_route", "action": "draw", "target": "borrow_route", "at": "25s", "cue": "stock-loan arrangement supports", "duration": "0.7s"},
        {"id": "flow_borrow_route", "action": "flow", "target": "borrow_route", "after": "draw_borrow_route", "duration": "1.1s", "color": "gold"},
        {"id": "show_paired_facts", "action": "fade-in", "target": ["short_harbor", "paired_with", "borrowed_harbor"], "at": "31s", "cue": "two facts together", "duration": "0.8s", "stagger": "0.18s"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "financing_and_margin",
      "duration": "40s",
      "layout": {"type": "center", "gap": "large", "align": "center"},
      "auto_visible": false,
      "show_progress_bar": false,
      "narration": "The prime broker may also lend the fund part of the money supporting its positions. That is secured financing. The fund provides capital and collateral, and the prime broker monitors the cushion protecting the loan. Suppose Harbor rises instead of falling. The short loses money, so that cushion shrinks. The prime broker may ask the fund to add collateral or reduce the position. The exact rules vary, but the reason is simple: the loan must remain protected as the value of the account changes.",
